## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates governance design capabilities for small remote teams, focusing on beginner-friendly processes that balance innovation with stability; emphasizes risk management, stakeholder communication, and scalable automation.

## Key Concepts
- Semantic versioning methodology
- Deprecation policy frameworks
- Automated compatibility testing
- Feature flag rollbacks
- Partner communication protocols

## Code Example
```javascript
// Version compatibility validator
function isCompatible(currentVersion, targetVersion) {
  const [cMA, cMi, cPa] = currentVersion.split('.').map(Number);
  const [tMA, tMi, tPa] = targetVersion.split('.').map(Number);

  // Major version changes are breaking
  if (cMA !== tMA) return false;

  // Minor version changes are backward compatible
  if (cMi > tMi) return false;

  return true;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a pragmatic, scalable program that links people, process, and outcomes. Evaluates how to allocate limited time for long‑term health without killing velocity, and how to guard against gaming.

## Key Concepts

- Team health budgeting and non-delivery work
- Cross‑team governance in multi-time‑zone setups
- ROI metrics: defect density, cycle time, retention
- Anti-gaming controls and sunset reviews

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple scoring for health proposals
function scoreProposal(p) {
  const impact = p.impact * 0.4;
  const risk = (1 - p.timeliness) * 0.3;
  const effort = 1 / (p.effort + 0.01);
  return impact + risk + effort;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle proposals that seem high ROI but strain critical squads?
- What metrics would you track to ensure long-term health gains persist beyond one quarter?
